        "title": "Cancel opposites",
        "body": "The integers $-999,-998,\\ldots,999,1000$ are 2000 consecutive integers; the numbers from $-999$ to $999$ cancel in pairs, leaving $1000$. Consecutive integers with a given sum are unique (shifting by 1 changes the sum by 2000), so the greatest is 1000, with digit sum $1$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1**"
